                            <comment id="476131" author="paf0186" created="Fri, 24 Oct 2025 20:14:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve been looking at the original patch here comment and the design looks good to me.&#160; The basic approach of mapping things into the paycheck pages seems sound, and I think we can handle direct IO by simply forcing it to fall back to buffered IO when there is a degraded read, since degraded read are not performant anyway.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My only other concern is I want to be sure that we&apos;re locking all of the required components together, ie, not lock-read-unlock, lock-read-unlock, but lock-lock, read-read, unlock-unlock so we don&apos;t run into any issues with split reads when we eventually support writes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
